<title>USA: W. Virginia jobless rate drops to 7.8 pct in March.</title>
<headline>W. Virginia jobless rate drops to 7.8 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLESTON, W.Va. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Virginia's unemployment rate dipped to 7.8 percent in March from 8.7 percent in February, the state Bureau of Employment Programs said Thursday.</p>
<p>The rate was the lowest for March since 1979. Nonfarm employment rose by 9,000, with nearly every industry reporting gains.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
</text>
